      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have tried using the fix that was posted here:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1110offset-seated-position-on-rotated-stations\n\nbut this does not seem to do anything for the Y rotation of the player, so you will still be sat, rotated as though you had swivelled your chair to the left or right if you enter the seat looking anywhere other than directly ahead. I tried using:\n\nSeat.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(Vector3.zero)\n\nInstead of:\n\nSeat.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(0, Seat.eulerAngles.y, 0);\n\nBut they both seem to have the same effect. If anyone knows how to hack around the Y rotation, please let me know!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
