      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It gets your forward vector from the direction you're looking at the moment you enter the station, if you don't turn your head after you enter, you will be looking forward.\n\nIn order to fix this you'd need a way of determining what direction is 'forward' for the player without using head rotation. Hip tracker maybe, but almost no one has them, and it may also suffer from the same issue(probably less though).\n\nThe way I deal with it personally is play space rotation.\n\nSome way to adjust rotation after entering a station is probably the best solution.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
